# The engine, bundled for Deno. Generated by scripts/build-functions.mjs and
# rebuilt by `npm run functions:build`; committing it would commit a build
# product that silently disagrees with the source it was built from.
#
# Its sibling `engine.d.ts` is NOT ignored, and the difference is worth stating.
# That file holds no compiled code — it is nine lines re-exporting the original
# sources, so an editor and a typechecker opened on the function see the real
# types. Ignoring it meant `npm run typecheck` could not resolve the bundle on a
# fresh clone, which is exactly the machine CI is.
supabase/functions/_shared/engine.js
